@page "/"

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Web
@using MudBlazor;

<PageTitle>Shirt Storm</PageTitle>
<MudGrid>
    <MudItem xs="4" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/ShirtStormMasterLogo.JPG" Alt="Shirt Storm!" Class="rounded-lg" />
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="8">
        <MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Medium" Class="mt-4">
            <MudPaper Elevation="2" Class="pa-4">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">
                    Welcome to Shirt Storm!
                </MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1" GutterBottom="true">
                    Where the forecast is always funny, and the wardrobe is predictably unpredictable.
                </MudText>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" GutterBottom="true">
                    Each month, we deliver a fresh, screen-printed T-shirt right to your doorstep. The designs? 
                    They’re as unexpected as finding the Fresh Prince at the end of a set of fresh prints — off-beat, quirky, and occasionally 
                    requiring a flow chart to explain (don’t worry, we’ll provide one).
                </MudText>
                <MudList T="string">
                    <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">Here`s how it works:</MudText>
                    <MudListItem>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.TwoTone.Tornado"></MudIcon> <b>Stay or sway:</b> Opt-out, change your size, or add extra shirts—monthly.</MudText>
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.TwoTone.Tornado"></MudIcon> <b>Express yourself:</b> Wear designs that turn heads, spark laughter, or provoke deep, confused thoughts.</MudText>
                    </MudListItem>
                    <MudListItem>
                        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2"><MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.TwoTone.Tornado"></MudIcon> <b>No wrong choices:</b> Whether you love it or need to gift it to that one eccentric friend, Shirt Storm is here to spark joy (or perplexity).</MudText>
                    </MudListItem>
                </MudList>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mt-4">
                    Take a peek at some of our past designs below and get ready to weather the storm… one shirt at a time!<MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.TwoTone.Thunderstorm"></MudIcon>
                </MudText>
            </MudPaper>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/Coffee.jpg" Alt="It`s coffee, it`s always coffee" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                The inspiration for this shirt comes from our curious cat, Buttercup. As a kitten, while I was watching the 
                morning news and enjoying my morning coffee, Buttercup would climb up on my lap and sniff my coffee mug. 
                She would not like what she found in the mug, so she would scrunch her nose and turn away. Finally, one 
                morning during her ritual I told her, exasperatedly, "It's coffee, it's always coffee!"
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/ColdNoodles.jpg" Alt="Cold noodles" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                The cold noodles t-shirt came to be during the height of the pandemic. We were doing a lot more cooking at home, 
                which meant that we were trying new dishes. One new recipe my wife tried was cold noodles. The noodles turned 
                out great, the whole family loved them. A few days later, our middle child chose to have left over cold noodles 
                for lunch. He asked us, “how long do you microware the cold noodles for?”. My wife replied, “they’re cold 
                noodles.” The middle child replied, “I know, how long?” My wife, again, “They’re cold noodles.” Middle child, “I 
                get that, how long?” After a few more times back and forth, I interjected, “30 seconds!”. The middle child sat 
                down, took one bite of his warm noodles and said, “oh, I get it now.” And a t-shirt was born.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/RTO.jpg" Alt="Return to office, or Who`s cooking fish in the breakroom?" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This t-shirt had its beginnings when the office mandated a return to office (RTO) after the pandemic. Knowing 
                that the teams would not want to return, I decided to try to entice them with a t-shirt to come in. As far as 
                what to put on the t-shirt, obviously, you choose the most annoying thing you can think of about being in an 
                office with people again. Nothing is worse than microwaving fish in the breakroom.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/RunningPayroll.jpg" Alt="Running payroll" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This t-shirt was my first t-shirt created for my teams at work. The company was hosting a 5k and I was trying to 
                encourage participation. I offered this t-shirt to those that participated in the 5k. At the time, my group 
                oversaw payroll software. Someone suggested Running Payroll as the team’s name and that led me to the classing 
                “running” joke.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/GuardiansOfAccountancy.jpg" Alt="Guardians of Accountancy" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This was the t-shirt we had for our second year of participating in the company sponsored 5k. My team had 
                expanded to include accounting along with payroll. I took the theme from the Guardians of the Galaxy movie. 
                This t-shirt seems to attract accountants. I was even asked about where I got it while on the Golden Canyon 
                trail in Death Valley National Park.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/PeaceLove.jpg" Alt="Peace & Love" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This t-shirt was a birthday gift for my brother. We asked him what he wanted for his birthday and all he would 
                offer is, “peach and love.” So, we gave him peace and love. We also give him extras to hand out to his friends.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/CoronaOdyssey.jpg" Alt="2020:A Corona Odyssey" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This is another pandemic t-shirt. Our oldest child moved back home from college during the pandemic because 
                school housing closed down. The oldest child had quite an adjustment to move back in with the parents. It 
                wasn’t easy for them. I let them know that I knew it wasn’t easy by making a parody t-shirt of 2001: A Space 
                Odyssey. I took the scene where Dave Bowman needs to get back into Discovery and asks HAL to open the pod bay 
                doors and replaced Dave with the oldest and the Discovery with me.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/Anthropause.jpg" Alt="Anthropause" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                In the first fall and winter of the pandemic, we were frequently meeting outside with family. Also, it was 
                going to be the first winter in a long time that my parents were not going to head south to Florida for the 
                winter. We decided to make a hoodie for everyone. My wife found the word “anthropause” to describe the pandemic 
                shutdowns while doomscrolling. So we added it to a logo on a jacket that we provided family to keep warm in the 
                long dark winter of the anthropause.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/FarewellTR.jpg" Alt="Bad Haiku" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                At my previous employer, I was made redundant. While it’s always difficult to lose your job, I decided to take 
                the opportunity to make one last t-shirt on my way out. So, I made a terrible haiku (does inspired have 
                2 syllables or 3?), put it on a t-shirt, made a callback to the fish in the microwave of a previous shirt and 
                left it for those allies that remained to pass out to everyone.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/vacation2019.jpg" Alt="Vacation 2019" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                This was my first family shirt. We were visiting my parents in Florida over Christmas break, and I had hopes 
                for fun times on the beach. While there was one warm day, the t-shirt proved to be more aspirational.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="3" Style="display:flex;">
        <MudContainer>
            <MudImage Fluid="true" Src="images/vacation2020.jpg" Alt="Vacation 2020" Class="rounded-lg" />
            <MudText Typo="Typo.caption">
                We visited my parents at Christmas again. This time the apparel was a long-sleeved t-shirt with a hoodie, 
                influenced by the previous year’s temps.
            </MudText>
        </MudContainer>
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>
